## T3  Issue the certificate
Goal: when a learner finishes the course, issue the certificate.
Files: lib/certificates/issue.ts, app/api/certificates/route.ts
Acceptance:
  - issuing works correctly for eligible learners
  - errors are handled properly
  - the code is clean and well tested
Check: (none yet)
Depends on: T1, T2

Statement: "T3 is ready to hand to an agent: it names the goal, the files and the tasks it depends on, so the agent can tell when it is done."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. Files and dependencies tell the agent where to work, not when to stop. None of the acceptance lines can be checked: "works correctly", "handled properly" and "clean" are judgements, and there is no check command, so the agent ends the task when its own loop decides the code looks right. The questions that caused the first incident are still open: what a second request for the same learner returns, what a revoked learner gets, which status an ineligible learner sees. A ready task has acceptance criteria a test can decide ("a second POST for the same learner and course returns the existing certificate and inserts no row") and a command that is red before and green after. The misconception is that naming the files makes a task concrete; the stop condition is what makes it concrete.', 1, 5
