    SELECT (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_acp_121'), 'From tasks.md:

## T1  Eligibility check (pure function, no I/O)
Files: lib/certificates/eligibility.ts, tests/certificates/eligibility.test.ts
Check: npx vitest run tests/certificates/eligibility.test.ts

The agent''s branch for T1:

$ git diff --stat origin/main...agent/t1-eligibility
 app/api/certificates/route.ts                |  64 ++++
 db/migrations/20261026_001_certificates.sql  |  21 +
 lib/certificates/eligibility.ts              |  48 +++
 lib/certificates/pdf.ts                      | 117 +++++++
 tests/certificates/eligibility.test.ts       |  95 +++++
 5 files changed, 345 insertions(+)

$ npx vitest run tests/certificates/eligibility.test.ts
 Tests  14 passed (14)

Statement: "The route, the migration and the PDF code are outside T1 and should be split out or reverted before T1 is reviewed, even though the T1 check passes."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. T1 lists two files; the diff has five. The route, the migration and the PDF generator belong to later tasks with their own acceptance criteria and checks, and none of them is exercised by the T1 check, so a green T1 run says nothing about them. Merging them now means 200 unreviewed lines arrive with a passing test as cover, and the later tasks start from code nobody planned or reviewed. Ask the agent to keep only the T1 files (or revert the rest) and treat the extra work as input for T2-T4. The misconception is that extra work done "for free" is a bonus; outside the task it is unreviewed scope.', 2, 5
