Session summary, task "Fix the typo in the leaderboard page title":
  skill metadata loaded   4 skills, about 300 tokens
  files read              app/leaderboard/page.tsx
  commands run            npm run lint

Statement: "Every session in this repository spends context on the 610 lines of reference/naming.md, so the file should be cut down or merged into SKILL.md."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. The session summary shows what was actually loaded: the short metadata of four skills and one page file. reference/naming.md is read only when the agent follows the line in SKILL.md that points to it, which happens for a migration task, not for a typo fix. That is the point of putting long reference material in its own file. Merging it into SKILL.md would make things worse: the 610 lines would then be loaded every time the skill is used, even when no new name is needed. The misconception is that everything in a skill folder is loaded into every session; check the session''s files read instead of guessing.', 2, 5
