       ((SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_coding_acp_212'), 2, 'Split the text into lines once, find the index of the first and the closing "---" line, then handle the frontmatter lines and the body separately. Check the quote stripping and the letter case of "use when".'),
       ((SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_coding_acp_212'), 3, 'A similar check on another file: for "---\ntitle: ''Release 1.3''\n---\n" the frontmatter has one key, title, with the value Release 1.3 (quotes removed), and the body is "" - so a rule "body must not be empty" reports it. The line "  owner: platform" starts with spaces, so it is a nested value and is skipped.');
