15:40:02 verdict  allow (matched "npm test")
15:40:19 exit 0   (tests: 214 passed)

Statement: "Because the check only looked at the start of the string, it approved the whole line, including piping a downloaded script into bash."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. startsWith sees the line as one opaque string, so anything after "npm test" rides along: && runs curl after the tests pass (they did, 214 passed), and | bash executes whatever the server returns, with the agent''s permissions. A command policy has to split the line the way the shell will - on &&, ||, ;, | and &, outside quotes - and judge every segment, denying the line if any segment is denied. The misconception is that an allow list of "safe commands" is safe by itself; it is only as good as the parser that decides what the command is.', 2, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_acp_311') AND order_index = 2)
    RETURNING id
)
