Statement: "This job is safe enough because it runs on a fresh GitHub-hosted virtual machine that is thrown away when the job ends."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. A fresh virtual machine protects the runner''s disk from the next job; it does not limit what the job''s credentials can do while it runs. Here the agent''s shell sees the production DATABASE_URL, so any command it decides to run (a migration, a cleanup script, a test that truncates tables) reaches production, and permissions: write-all lets the job token push commits and change issues, pull requests and releases. There is also no timeout-minutes, so a stuck agent runs until GitHub''s default job limit of 360 minutes and keeps spending AI tokens. The misconception is to confuse an isolated machine with least privilege: isolation is about where code runs, privilege is about what its credentials and network can reach.', 1, 5
