Statement: "With this setup the agent can open a pull request, but its change reaches main only after a person from @codedev/platform approves it and the test check passes."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. The job token can only read the repository, the database is a throwaway Postgres container with test data, and the only write path is the script that pushes an agent/* branch and opens a pull request with the agent app''s token. The rules on main require a pull request, one approval from a code owner (a team of people, so the app cannot approve its own change) and the test check, with no bypass. The budget (30 minutes, at most 3 USD) bounds a stuck run, and the transcript artifact shows what the agent did. A human merging is the last gate, not the only one; each of the other limits makes that review smaller and safer.', 2, 5
